.TH QFW-SLURM-GATEWAY 8 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qfw-slurm-gateway \- serve and inspect QFw Slurm reservations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-slurm-gateway
.BI --config " path"
.RI [ --log-level " level" ]
.B serve
.br
.B qfw-slurm-gateway
.BI --config " path"
.B status
.I job-id
.br
.B qfw-slurm-gateway
.BI --config " path"
.B list
.br
.B qfw-slurm-gateway
.BI --config " path"
.B check
.RI [ --service " service-id" ]...
.br
.B qfw-slurm-gateway
.BI --config " path"
.B retry-release
.I job-id
.RI [ --reason " code" ]
.RI [ --request-id " id" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-slurm-gateway
provides the authenticated QSGP endpoint used by the Slurm lifecycle helper
and diagnostic driver. It verifies job identity through slurmctld,
resolves exact QPM services through DEFw, and journals reserve and release
operations in SQLite.
.PP
Commands that contact the DEFw directory or a QPM must run inside an
initialized DEFw process. Use
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway-launch (8)
or the installed systemd service. The read-only
.B status
and
.B list
commands access only the journal and may run directly.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read the protected gateway YAML file. This option is required.
.TP
.BI --log-level " level"
Set
.BR DEBUG ,
.BR INFO ,
.BR WARNING ,
or
.BR ERROR .
The default is
.BR INFO .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the QSGP listener until SIGINT or SIGTERM. Under systemd, readiness and
stopping state are sent through
.BR sd_notify (3).
.TP
.BI status " job-id"
Print the allocation, reservation rows, response record, and lifecycle state
as JSON.
.TP
.B list
Print all nonterminal allocations as JSON.
.TP
.BI check " [--service service-id]..."
Open the journal, initialize DEFw, and resolve every named QPM. The JSON result
includes each runtime ID and directory generation.
.TP
.BI retry-release " job-id"
Retry every nonterminal reservation for one allocation. Use
.BI --reason " code"
to select the release reason and
.BI --request-id " id"
to reuse a known request identity. Otherwise a nonzero unsigned request ID is
generated.
.SH JOURNAL STATES
An allocation may be
.BR reserving ,
.BR reserved ,
.BR releasing ,
.BR release-incomplete ,
or
.BR released .
Unresolved release results remain journaled for an operator retry. The gateway
does not report them as released.
.SH SECURITY
The gateway accepts only MUNGE-authenticated sender UIDs listed by its
configuration or otherwise authorized for the verified Slurm job. QPM
credentials remain inside QPMd and are not stored in the gateway journal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qfw-slurm/gateway.yaml
Protected listener, authentication, Slurm, QFw, and journal configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/qfw-slurm-gateway/reservations.sqlite3
Default durable journal path in the packaged example.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-slurm-driver (1),
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-slurm (7),
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway-launch (8),
.BR qfw-slurm-bb (8)
